    {
      "id": "claim_59848b286bfc46f79ed56ff9c60db25a",
      "statement": "The `dev` extra is where pytest and the analysis toolchain (ruff, mutmut, diff-cover, hypothesis, pytest-randomly, pytest-cov, jsonschema) are declared; the project's runtime dependencies are only ruamel.yaml, rich, pip-audit and typer. Plain `uv sync` therefore installs no pytest and the suite fails with a missing command rather than a test result.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pyproject.toml#L5-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:76cd8d3e640c99f3ea544f4de226ac585796533a5643ed4307d6a652f2059041:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_762f77ba63b84de39a3d1fdfa7c30eec",
      "statement": "The test suite is invoked through `tools/run-tests.sh` (whole suite, one file, or filters like `-k install -x`) and never as a hand-composed mise/uv/pytest line: the script handles worktree setup, is idempotent, and absorbs the per-branch venv outside the repo, the mandatory `--extra dev`, and mise's untrusted-config refusal; the live CI workflow invokes the same script so CI and a developer box run the same thing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L99-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f1a2b8947768097af195c4ff26e3afd2bfde826ed14d94ca322091dd43e732a3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://CONTRIBUTING.md#L170-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc1e66f24fb6596822a866550ffb9deed9de7fef1cd753c07becac624e716fd7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7343fd0b431d49ff8e2efdff44dfe902",
      "statement": "`mise.toml` keeps the venv outside the repo (one per branch via UV_PROJECT_ENVIRONMENT under ~/.local/share/harnessed/venvs/<branch>/.venv) to avoid corrupting a .venv under a podman bind mount, and pins UV_PYTHON to 3.12, the floor of requires-python, so local runs exercise the interpreter CI's default job uses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mise.toml#L26-L41",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b68591a1e0b7eedaa815d34fe41ef47ab603f7d92e8d80a6d62158b6e899cf6b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d1eb543f0c5a40dd90dbc6052e3e309a",
      "statement": "`tools/preflight.sh` is run before every PR because `uv run pytest -q` covers only one of four CI gates: it runs pytest then `ruff` → `pyright` → `shellcheck` in CI's exact order and with CI's exact lint argv, with `--all` adding the catalog pin check and `--no-tests` running the lint layers only. Its one deliberate divergence from CI is that it runs every gate even after an earlier one fails and reports each skipped layer by name.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://CLAUDE.md#L99-L115",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f1a2b8947768097af195c4ff26e3afd2bfde826ed14d94ca322091dd43e732a3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://CONTRIBUTING.md#L170-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc1e66f24fb6596822a866550ffb9deed9de7fef1cd753c07becac624e716fd7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d1e70e50ce96431686a8d137460fe4bc",
      "statement": "A green pytest run is not end-to-end proof: the hermetic suite runs no `podman build` and no `harnessed container-run`, and contributors must record the baseline test count before a change because a count drop is a regression even when new tests pass.",
