    {
      "id": "claim_0c617dbdf4e54c97abcdf5f8fe61d8ec",
      "statement": "The package declares exactly two console entrypoints in pyproject.toml — `harnessed` → `harnessed.launcher:main` (the Typer verb surface that drives podman) and `harnessed-tools` → `harnessed.cli:main` (the emit-only assembler plus the `test`/`scan`/persist/lint subcommands) — and that split is why launcher-only bugs do not reproduce under `harnessed-tools` while emit modules must stay runtime-free.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pyproject.toml#L17-L19",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:90c7d5e9c7479cdc7651c6b0e02c74422cd67da0715172470ac821543070ba80:"
